---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { contactUrl } from "@/lib/present";
---

<Layout
  title="How SignalScout Radar works"
  description="How Radar finds public posts where people ask which product to buy, what it shows, and how to have a post removed."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[760px] px-4 pt-12 sm:px-8">
    <p class="text-[0.8125rem] font-semibold tracking-wider text-primary uppercase">How it works</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] sm:text-4xl">What Radar does</h1>

    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-secondary-foreground">
      <p>
        Every hour Radar searches Reddit and X for public posts with phrases like
        <em>"can anyone recommend"</em>, <em>"what do you use"</em> and <em>"is it worth buying"</em>.
      </p>
      <p>
        A simple text rule sets most of them aside for free. An AI model reads the rest and answers
        two questions: does the author ask which product to use or buy, and what kind of product is it?
        It also writes one line that says what the person wants.
      </p>
      <p>
        Radar is built on the open-source engine of
        <a href="https://www.signalscout.run" class="font-semibold text-primary hover:underline">SignalScout</a>.
        SignalScout does the same job for one product: it finds only the posts that fit what you sell,
        scores them, and explains why.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What Radar shows, and what it does not</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-secondary-foreground">
      <li>A short excerpt of each post and a link to the original.</li>
      <li>No usernames, no profile pictures, and no copy of the full post.</li>
      <li>Nothing older than 30 days.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="remove" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Remove a post</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-secondary-foreground">
      If a post on Radar is yours, or you want it gone for any other reason,
      <a href={contactUrl} class="font-semibold text-primary hover:underline">send us its link</a>.
      We remove it, and Radar will not show it again.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
